    <solution><p>A unit vector is computed by dividing the original vector by its magnitude.</p>
<p>The magnitude of a vector <m>\langle x,y,z\rangle</m> is its length, computed with the formula <m>\sqrt{x^2+y^2+z^2}</m>.  In this case, that computation yields:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{\sqrt{-17^2 - 16^2+18^2}=\sqrt{289+256+324}=\sqrt{869}=29.47881}</m></p>
<p>So we can now finish the unit vector computation, as follows.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{\frac{\langle -17,-16,18 \rangle}{29.47881}=\langle -0.57669,-0.54276,0.61061 \rangle}</m></p>
</solution>
